From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:47:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: add KIP OOB pairing
 node for SP11

The Surface Pro 11 Flex Keyboard exposes a Bluetooth out-of-band pairing
channel on KIP HID instance 9 (PID 0C8F). It carries the Microsoft
"Bluetooth OOB Coupling" HID collection (vendor usage page 0xFFF4), which
a host uses to hand the keyboard its Bluetooth address and a pairing key
over the wired connector, so the keyboard can subsequently be used
detached over Bluetooth.

The instance was not registered, so the device never appeared and there
was no way to pair the keyboard for detached use except by importing a
bond created by another operating system.

Register it for the SP11 node group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 .../platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c   | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index d37a7e4c6b02..2192e4e6389a 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -215,6 +215,17 @@ static const struct software_node ssam_node_hid_kip_fwupd = {
 	.parent = &ssam_node_hub_kip,
 };
 
+/* HID device instance 9 (KIP hub, Bluetooth OOB pairing channel).
+ *
+ * Exposes the Microsoft "Bluetooth OOB Coupling" collection (HID usage page
+ * 0xFFF4) used to hand the host's Bluetooth address and a pairing key to a
+ * detachable keyboard over the wired link, so it can then be used detached.
+ */
+static const struct software_node ssam_node_hid_kip_oobpair = {
+	.name = "ssam:01:15:02:09:00",
+	.parent = &ssam_node_hub_kip,
+};
+
 /* Tablet-mode switch via POS subsystem. */
 static const struct software_node ssam_node_pos_tablet_switch = {
 	.name = "ssam:01:26:01:00:01",
@@ -415,6 +426,7 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp11[] = {
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_penstash,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_touchpad,
 	&ssam_node_hid_kip_fwupd,
+	&ssam_node_hid_kip_oobpair,
 	&ssam_node_hid_sam_sensors,
 	&ssam_node_kip_tablet_switch,
 	NULL,
